Short:        TCP/IP stack with modern TCP and Linux tools
Author:       Riptide developers
Uploader:     farsonic@gmail.com (Riptide)
Type:         comm/tcp
Version:      @VERSION@
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.0
Requires:     68020+, a SANA-II network driver (or uaenet.device)
Distribution: Aminet
URL:          https://github.com/farsonic/riptide

Riptide is a TCP/IP stack for AmigaOS 3.x on the 68020 to 68060.

* publishes bsdsocket.library 4 (the AmiTCP API, all 46 functions),
  riptide.library and usergroup.library while it runs
* modern TCP after the Linux stack: CUBIC with HyStart, SACK, RACK-TLP,
  PRR, F-RTO, timestamps, window scaling, ECN, buffer auto-tuning
* SANA-II devices (Ethernet or point-to-point) and MNI drivers, a DHCP
  client and a DNS resolver
* Linux style tools: ip, ifconfig, route, arp, netstat, ping,
  traceroute, host, sysctl, hostname, nc, an ftp client, speedtest
  (a speedtest.net bandwidth test after speedtest-cli) and rtdiag
* RiptidePrefs, a settings editor (GadTools) for riptide.conf: interface,
  DHCP or static address, names, DNS, time, TCP; keeps comments and
  lines it does not know
* diagnostics for slow transfers: packet capture to pcap files,
  profiler, debug log, per-connection TCP details (netstat -T), driver
  counters (ip -s link) and rtdiag, which collects all of it
* one binary for the 68020 to 68060 with hand-written checksum and copy
  routines

Installation: double-click Install_Riptide (standard Amiga Installer).
It copies the programs to C:, writes ENVARC:Riptide/riptide.conf for the
emulator's uaenet.device with DHCP (or another SANA-II device / a static
address) and adds Riptide to S:User-Startup. See Riptide/ReadMe and
Riptide/Docs/AMIGA.md.

Under FS-UAE use uae_sana2 = 1 and network_card = a2065; turn off the
emulator's bsdsocket.library emulation (WinUAE and FS-UAE).

